#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119546 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "d5a81b39-421e-55c3-90de-d9f4e6489cd5" :question/math-academy-id "e-4795" :question/problem "Determine if $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/assets/df4f126da2ab3a0661bcb7dc18bb1e5eae8cd48d5c5a1464ea580ccc439195d6.png)" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = 3,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\mathbf{b}$ does *not* lie in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119547 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "94a17888-dcef-58e0-8147-0dec3745f136" :question/math-academy-id "e-4799" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\;\\Pi \\,:\\, \\mathbf{r}=s \\mathbf{b} + t \\mathbf{c}, \\, t,s \\in \\mathbb{R},$ where  $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1, 4, 5 \\rangle, \\mathbf{c} = \\langle 2, 4, 6 \\rangle$ and  $\\mathbf{u}= \\langle 2, 10, 12 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u} \\in \\Pi$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+2t=2 \\\\ 4s+4t=10 \\\\ 5s+6t=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+2t=2 \\\\ -4t=2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-4t = 2 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad t = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s+2t & =2 \\\\ s+2(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =2 \\\\ s-1 & =2 \\\\ s & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=3, \\, t=-\\dfrac{1}{2},$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $\\Pi.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=3\\mathbf{b} - \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{c}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119595 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "21a6808a-5b1c-5b1d-9bd4-da605fb6d920" :question/math-academy-id "e-6218" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082953/assets/399d7fed8338969b654454d30f2ee661edbd52b3a61d065f33972be21996e188.png)" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=13 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{14}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-16{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = k-11$. Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0 = k-11 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad k=11.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb615b07-46fa-5c9b-bd12-0e4983282da6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321585} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee33ddf-b597-56c5-a884-20d5c9cabffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321586} {:answer/id #uuid "14ed59de-3ac0-5711-9017-c18c6857811b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321587} {:answer/id #uuid "5d4ff864-903f-56ea-9b99-e95f93374b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321588} {:answer/id #uuid "a988dae2-4651-5294-a8e4-88f9fa56f040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14ed59de-3ac0-5711-9017-c18c6857811b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321587} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eb72595-3a95-5b00-ba54-0bcdfa25110c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6dd9a94f-9ad6-5f46-b62e-569214d55f1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105208" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -5 & -17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3(-2)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=9.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 9\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=9\\cdot (-2)=-18.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c69efb4-3276-5df3-9679-903de10ad9c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387413} {:answer/id #uuid "31c0df89-339a-5ed8-a572-3354dd2c34ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387414} {:answer/id #uuid "16ab4253-48bf-583d-b015-b97f6da4eaec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387415} {:answer/id #uuid "35ffd69d-f9fe-59c5-959c-8a79eb4306fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387416} {:answer/id #uuid "4a601237-e469-5910-b78e-92d971d65588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a601237-e469-5910-b78e-92d971d65588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387417} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7f6592d-4257-5e06-90ae-710df775cbea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da64bb93-914e-5229-bb6d-b7d97e6fa1bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-105248" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,-4,2⟩$, $c=⟨3,-10,2⟩$, and  $u=⟨-2,5,0⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+3t=-2 \\\\ -4s-10t=5 \\\\ 2s+2t=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -10 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-2,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ed90633-8e5a-5726-821a-bfd0ae6ce04f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387420} {:answer/id #uuid "7646de9a-cf05-56f0-aed4-a48a532e6dea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387421} {:answer/id #uuid "97efbbd0-bccd-5f58-afc6-ffc659d046f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387422} {:answer/id #uuid "8a5ef1cf-0d8b-5af1-9139-8f8599e89357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387423} {:answer/id #uuid "4d952097-5fa9-566a-9550-bb82251b7981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d952097-5fa9-566a-9550-bb82251b7981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387424} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7297fef-03d0-5b08-a3fb-1b74d7b959e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "72980dd9-a084-58f4-8392-6327a30e9f96" :question/math-academy-id "q-105253" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,3,2⟩$, $c=⟨2,-1,-1⟩$, and  $u=⟨5,-5,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t=5 \\\\ 3s-t=-5 \\\\ 2s-t=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t=5 \\\\ t=2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+2t & =5 \\\\ -s+2(2) & =5 \\\\ -s+4 & =5 \\\\ s & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-1,\\,t=2,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-b+2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-1)\\cdot 2=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387425 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d857f2f-77a9-588d-a0a9-08e2017c4867" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387427} {:answer/id #uuid "c334db72-a81e-541a-9f28-0a829301718f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387428} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a06f1c-1838-562b-915d-f343b96cc0a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387429} {:answer/id #uuid "475fffa5-0d8e-54ee-a8dd-c638c63c2fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387430} {:answer/id #uuid "bb04a159-dc05-53fd-bd0e-f8f70b269f5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c334db72-a81e-541a-9f28-0a829301718f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387428} :answer-field/id #uuid "33923fde-d387-569f-8da2-cb09517cf247" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dc42dd0f-fa8b-5044-b147-6f3f5acbed6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105261" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,-1,3⟩$, $c=⟨-2,4,-3⟩$, and  $u=⟨3,-7,3⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-2t=3 \\\\ -s+4t=-7 \\\\ 3s-3t=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-2t=3 \\\\ t=-2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-2t & =3 \\\\ s-2(-2) & =3 \\\\ s+4 & =3 \\\\ s & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-1,\\,t=-2,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-b-2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-1)\\cdot (-2)=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387432 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24c3fae9-d3ae-502b-8f7f-fb40fb8de31c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387434} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb1c392-32e4-50f7-a8a3-2bc24529e6c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387435} {:answer/id #uuid "2cfc4d70-30ec-5784-974b-ba94c33f7351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387436} {:answer/id #uuid "3255ac99-a111-5467-9e29-dead55f06590" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387437} {:answer/id #uuid "dd405635-8c50-5edf-bac0-2737d2e738ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24c3fae9-d3ae-502b-8f7f-fb40fb8de31c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387434} :answer-field/id #uuid "e694556f-63c7-5042-b52f-ae798fc5ddb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "217990a1-bfab-5780-8ba0-05d1ef5c390b" :question/math-academy-id "q-34058" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-1=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot 1=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321618 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea4c1454-1b3f-5538-848a-5fd619152623" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321620} {:answer/id #uuid "94c7eda6-95b2-5699-9ecb-21fc7eedb7a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321621} {:answer/id #uuid "de4e7fc1-1202-5824-8901-d6141ce31e19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321622} {:answer/id #uuid "03c059cb-ba7a-56c2-b295-31bf1e79c393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321623} {:answer/id #uuid "d97435db-465c-5813-92b0-2de72eb9fdac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d97435db-465c-5813-92b0-2de72eb9fdac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321624} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4802b34-38f1-5390-8fff-a8dca2a5666e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfb9b107-bb38-574d-9d31-74a75b24630d" :question/math-academy-id "q-34115" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 31\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=31,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $b$ does *not* lie in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1885f6c6-1737-593d-a0b0-f40f204dfd3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348066} {:answer/id #uuid "d1920435-93cf-5231-beff-2dcd6353a8a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348067} {:answer/id #uuid "4824b77d-1f43-5121-ada6-096b6db97c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348068} {:answer/id #uuid "646dfa8c-ad7c-5650-a692-9a13b2e1f363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348069} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d5c801-e6e2-5bcb-bfe9-684cd229170a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1885f6c6-1737-593d-a0b0-f40f204dfd3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348066} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a9cffe4-2531-5e66-a9c8-2d9eb4d0f8e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2e640eb7-b1f9-5d7f-bab4-6d80d29a915a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34117" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 18 & -21 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-18{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+6(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+(-3){a}_{2}+(-1){a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+(-3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (-1)=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387439 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae24bfe2-518d-56e6-a395-177d2a46f8f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387441} {:answer/id #uuid "2d53c036-45b5-5d93-a198-e3f117255518" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387442} {:answer/id #uuid "6a787ffe-4733-5e57-8780-118497baaba9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387443} {:answer/id #uuid "4aabfd74-7929-521a-9ddb-a541df71ced9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387444} {:answer/id #uuid "f96780df-6bdb-5efc-b5dc-101e8b1dbf85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4aabfd74-7929-521a-9ddb-a541df71ced9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387444} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5113eef-6d87-5250-8552-90c8a6e833b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "57be7a53-3b34-5fc3-96ea-f6d1b5131a58" :question/math-academy-id "q-34212" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,7,-3⟩$, $c=⟨-8,10,-4⟩$, and  $u=⟨6,9,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-8t=6 \\\\ 7s+10t=9 \\\\ -3s-4t=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 10 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 66 & -33 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 66 & -33 \\\\ 0 & -28 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{66}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -28 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+28{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s-8t=6 \\\\ t=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-8t & =6 \\\\ s-8(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =6 \\\\ s+4 & =6 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b-\\frac{1}{2}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dbe4bda-3f55-5ece-b263-7c30604479a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387448} {:answer/id #uuid "2b60b66b-331b-5b38-ad62-9a1b72bf0d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387449} {:answer/id #uuid "3562c031-9e1e-5f09-97c3-af5b54c72ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387450} {:answer/id #uuid "81449efc-599a-5b1c-b2c0-8ee3a94cd34f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387451} {:answer/id #uuid "9486e2a8-7859-50f2-9be5-fea82c562106" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b60b66b-331b-5b38-ad62-9a1b72bf0d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387449} :answer-field/id #uuid "432f6afd-b6eb-52f9-9abb-870e3af64996" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "14df0726-4ddf-5979-a80e-ac9a921a2fc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-34218" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=6 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=-14 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 6 & -14 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=6 \\\\ {x}_{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(-2)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}+(-2){a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=2\\cdot 4\\cdot (-2)=-16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae44989b-7bf8-5c3e-bcb2-7a44520d1ff3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348073} {:answer/id #uuid "a908ed17-5d44-58f7-8b99-494b51e6e0a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348074} {:answer/id #uuid "873541a2-1bbb-5397-bc43-02cbfa9efd64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348075} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c2f712-5657-5e54-88da-49b70fb5dd7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348076} {:answer/id #uuid "ed587d61-4278-50c5-b0e5-2225f5d5a506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed587d61-4278-50c5-b0e5-2225f5d5a506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348077} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a7a6eaf-37f1-5d02-8771-868c922d65ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23910d50-0ae0-541a-a349-4d3875b18617" :question/math-academy-id "q-74558" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\nk=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b347c3da-126c-5853-a807-33d1065d5a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387455} {:answer/id #uuid "1fc62adf-ea57-50f8-bde5-452d410c45ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387456} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d07f82-aa57-5839-b9f9-bb9beb4eb283" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387457} {:answer/id #uuid "75443c33-1d46-5a70-8ae4-166b19dad67b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387458} {:answer/id #uuid "ba43cb17-3d34-5331-bd1f-dde4cc5b51af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75443c33-1d46-5a70-8ae4-166b19dad67b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387458} :answer-field/id #uuid "75b3faf2-ab55-5bd0-9acb-5add477557c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ada2a237-9557-5ce5-94c7-1c1c977d6e0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74559" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=-8 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 9 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 10 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 10 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 6 & k+6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-18.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-18\\,⇒\\,k=18.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120443 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1517a80-70f5-54ce-a9da-c604fa76fcd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119134} {:answer/id #uuid "1a38ace8-4251-5862-b732-4e1367f4471f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119135} {:answer/id #uuid "2d2a1ba4-2b21-53d3-9f32-b5797558dec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119136} {:answer/id #uuid "675ba5e9-f984-5195-b65a-b6e1ffc33392" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119137} {:answer/id #uuid "67c180bb-d09b-5310-a08c-2b63234e95f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d2a1ba4-2b21-53d3-9f32-b5797558dec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119136} :answer-field/id #uuid "b51687c7-9e34-586b-8606-390c3c88054f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f53bb678-a419-585c-a65e-c61f25afddb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-74560" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=-12 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=-10 \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+24\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+24.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+24\\,⇒\\,k=-24.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387460 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1341509a-6f87-5c3f-881f-74b4dc51dfab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387462} {:answer/id #uuid "2e697521-7e4c-573e-a773-adc0956231f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387463} {:answer/id #uuid "0f352382-a05a-52b4-8af8-a2aeb5d91b4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387464} {:answer/id #uuid "72463df5-0c4a-54aa-a992-2db48ab3cef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387465} {:answer/id #uuid "38a23b84-56dc-556b-95f0-b90136d8d3b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38a23b84-56dc-556b-95f0-b90136d8d3b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387466} :answer-field/id #uuid "a68e6986-93f0-5ddb-bc3d-0e21fa1da646" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387461}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a869a27c-0281-583b-9188-260c32bc33cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-74594" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -32 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -32 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-6.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-6\\,⇒\\,k=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387467 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d31a218e-3e10-5e7a-988e-687eaa85fdd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387469} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d9979d-3c30-5ff7-bbec-2e6a3890b26b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387470} {:answer/id #uuid "9c648914-378c-5059-9aab-c274cc294271" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387471} {:answer/id #uuid "277f8286-98ce-55e1-8e73-9c94a006b9cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387472} {:answer/id #uuid "294f2ada-1f7b-5719-bc0a-8d2176df0146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6d9979d-3c30-5ff7-bbec-2e6a3890b26b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387470} :answer-field/id #uuid "e621b626-d1c0-573c-8075-7e9dbf7d6013" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "904c48e4-0b9c-5c7e-bf91-b07b77859fe9" :question/math-academy-id "q-74597" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k+6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k+6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+4.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+4\\,⇒\\,k=-4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387474 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ca74f6d-7460-5497-b4e9-8f716497e891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387476} {:answer/id #uuid "7c32844e-2918-5110-b1f8-b802f26e43ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387477} {:answer/id #uuid "4bd3d188-2cc1-584d-a483-28aa2c599d10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387478} {:answer/id #uuid "949c7d37-ae91-5770-8114-649fa6ee66e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387479} {:answer/id #uuid "af2c40ca-62ce-55af-a8b5-9e60396e4812" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bd3d188-2cc1-584d-a483-28aa2c599d10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387478} :answer-field/id #uuid "a168f6d1-ae31-5105-9fe9-23b6b9cd78b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a339e4e-decb-5668-80f9-2bcd81514c71" :question/math-academy-id "q-74598" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,2,3⟩$, $c=⟨3,-7,-9⟩$, and  $u=⟨2,-3,-6⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t=2 \\\\ 2s-7t=-3 \\\\ 3s-9t=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t=2 \\\\ -t=1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-t=1\\,⟹\\,t=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+3t & =2 \\\\ -s+3(-1) & =2 \\\\ -s & =5 \\\\ s & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-5,\\,t=-1,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-5b-c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-5)\\cdot (-1)=5.$"}]}
